  "body": {
    "storage": {
      "value": "<h2>Purpose and Benefits</h2><p>Sometimes, we may have to store some documents as part of the forms. &nbsp;Bahmni supports scanning the documents using a webcam on your device and uploading them in a form. &nbsp;There are various document types that are supported like jpeg, pdf. &nbsp;</p><h2>Steps to configure documents in the form</h2><ol><li>Create a concept with the concept class as &quot;Image&quot;, concept datatype as &quot;<span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Complex&quot; and Handler as &quot;<span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">BinaryDataHandler&quot;</span></span></li><li>Add this newly created concept to any of your existing concept set which represents a form (i.e. this concept set should be part of &quot;All Observation Templates&quot;)</li><li>View the newly added field in the form. &nbsp;This field has a &quot;+&quot; button beside the label which will help you upload the images.</li><li>The value filled in the form can be seen on the Patient Dashboard corresponding to the relevant Observation Display control.</li></ol>",
      "representation": "storage",
      "embeddedContent": [],
      "_expandable": {
        "content": "/rest/api/content/42729508"
      }
    },
    "view": {
      "value": "<h2 id=\"AddingScannedDocumentstoForms-PurposeandBenefits\">Purpose and Benefits</h2><p>Sometimes, we may have to store some documents as part of the forms.  Bahmni supports scanning the documents using a webcam on your device and uploading them in a form.  There are various document types that are supported like jpeg, pdf.  </p><h2 id=\"AddingScannedDocumentstoForms-Stepstoconfiguredocumentsintheform\">Steps to configure documents in the form</h2><ol><li>Create a concept with the concept class as &quot;Image&quot;, concept datatype as &quot;<span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">Complex&quot; and Handler as &quot;<span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">BinaryDataHandler&quot;</span></span></li><li>Add this newly created concept to any of your existing concept set which represents a form (i.e. this concept set should be part of &quot;All Observation Templates&quot;)</li><li>View the newly added field in the form.  This field has a &quot;+&quot; button beside the label which will help you upload the images.</li><li>The value filled in the form can be seen on the Patient Dashboard corresponding to the relevant Observation Display control.</li></ol>",
      "representation": "view",
